#. world_info.csv: You have a series of executable actions. Pay at...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_ACTION_DESC"
msgstr ""
"You have a series of executable actions. Pay attention to the effects, "
"restrictions, regions, and time of actions."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_ACTION_NAME"
msgstr "Action"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_ACTION_TITLE"
msgstr "Action"

#. world_info.csv: Every uncertain period of time, there will be a...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_AUCTION_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Every uncertain period of time, there will be an auction organized by a "
"mysterious person, perhaps selling good goods."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_AUCTION_NAME"
msgstr "Auction"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_AUCTION_TITLE"
msgstr "Auction"

#. world_info.csv: Survival of the fittest; realm suppression is h...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_BATTLE_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Survival of the fittest; realm suppression is huge, high-realm cultivators "
"have an absolute advantage over low-realm ones. If the opponent dies, the "
"winner can plunder the loser's belongings."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_BATTLE_NAME"
msgstr "Battle"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_BATTLE_TITLE"
msgstr "Battle"

#. world_info.csv: Cultivation accumulates power until the current...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_CULTIVATION_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Cultivation accumulates power until the current rank reaches its bottleneck."
" Breakthroughs can succeed or fail; success advances the character to the "
"next rank, while failure may carry a cost."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_CULTIVATION_NAME"
msgstr "Cultivation"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_CULTIVATION_TITLE"
msgstr "Cultivation"

#. world_info.csv: HP dropping below 0 also causes death.
msgid "WORLD_INFO_DEATH_DESC"
msgstr "HP dropping below 0 also causes death."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_DEATH_NAME"
msgstr "Death"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_DEATH_TITLE"
msgstr "Death"

#. world_info.csv: Weapons, auxiliary equipment, and elixirs provi...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_EQUIPMENT_AND_ELIXIR_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Weapons, auxiliary equipment, and elixirs provide extra bonuses. High-grade "
"equipment and suitable elixirs can greatly improve a cultivator's survival "
"and combat ability."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_EQUIPMENT_AND_ELIXIR_NAME"
msgstr "Equipment & Elixir"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_EQUIPMENT_AND_ELIXIR_TITLE"
msgstr "Equipment & Elixir"

#. world_info.csv: This is a cultivation world where many cultivat...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_INTRO_DESC"
msgstr "This is a cultivation world where many cultivators compete and conflicts rage on all sides."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_INTRO_NAME"
msgstr "Introduction"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_INTRO_TITLE"
msgstr "Introduction"

#. world_info.csv: Every character has a lifespan limit. When life...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_LIFESPAN_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Every character has a lifespan limit. When lifespan is exhausted, death "
"follows; realm breakthroughs usually extend lifespan, while failed "
"breakthroughs may shorten it."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_LIFESPAN_NAME"
msgstr "Lifespan"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_LIFESPAN_TITLE"
msgstr "Lifespan"

#. world_info.csv: Different orthodoxies have different cultivatio...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_ORTHODOXY_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Different orthodoxies have different cultivation methods. Taoists respire, "
"Martial Artists practice Body Tempering, Buddhists meditate, and Confucians "
"educate the people."

#. world_info.csv:
msgid "WORLD_INFO_ORTHODOXY_NAME"
msgstr "Orthodoxy"

#. world_info.csv: Orthodoxy
msgid "WORLD_INFO_ORTHODOXY_TITLE"
msgstr "Orthodoxy"

#. world_info.csv: The world's underlying standard realms, from we...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_REALM_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The world's underlying standard realms, from weak to strong, are Qi "
"Refinement, Foundation Establishment, Core Formation, and Nascent Soul. Each"
" realm has Early, Middle, and Late stages. Different traditions may use "
"aliases, but rules are calculated by this standard sequence."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_REALM_NAME"
msgstr "Realm"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_REALM_TITLE"
msgstr "Realm"

#. world_info.csv: Different regions have different effects; doing...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_REGION_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Different regions have different effects; doing the right thing in the right"
" region yields twice the result with half the effort."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_REGION_NAME"
msgstr "Region"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_REGION_TITLE"
msgstr "Region"

#. world_info.csv: Spirit roots are composed of five elements (Met...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_ROOT_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Spirit roots are composed of five elements (Metal, Wood, Water, Fire, "
"Earth), divided into Single, Dual, and Heavenly Spirit Roots. Five elements "
"interaction: Metal overcomes Wood, Wood overcomes Earth, Earth overcomes "
"Water, Water overcomes Fire, Fire overcomes Metal. Heavenly Spirit Root "
"contains all five elements and has an extra bonus during breakthrough. "
"Cultivation efficiency is highest in regions matching one's own spirit root "
"attribute."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_ROOT_NAME"
msgstr "Spirit Root"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_ROOT_TITLE"
msgstr "Spirit Root"

#. world_info.csv: Secret realms open every few years. Entering a ...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECRET_REALM_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Secret realms open every few years. Entering a secret realm may encounter "
"danger, but may also obtain high-level artifacts and techniques."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECRET_REALM_NAME"
msgstr "Secret Realm"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECRET_REALM_TITLE"
msgstr "Secret Realm"

#. world_info.csv: A shelter for cultivators. Joining a sect allow...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECT_DESC"
msgstr ""
"A shelter for cultivators. Joining a sect allows learning unique techniques "
"and gaining protection from fellow disciples; rogue cultivators are free but"
" lack resources."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECT_NAME"
msgstr "Sect"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECT_TITLE"
msgstr "Sect"

#. world_info.csv: In city regions, you can buy Qi Refinement-grad...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_SHOPPING_DESC"
msgstr ""
"In city regions, you can buy Qi Refinement-grade elixirs and weapons. "
"Purchased elixirs are consumed immediately to strengthen the character; "
"purchased weapons can switch the character to a more suitable weapon type."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SHOPPING_NAME"
msgstr "Shopping"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SHOPPING_TITLE"
msgstr "Shopping"

#. world_info.csv: The common currency of the cultivation world. C...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_SPIRIT_STONE_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The common currency of the cultivation world. Can be used to buy artifacts "
"and elixirs, obtained through gathering, trading, or plundering."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SPIRIT_STONE_NAME"
msgstr "Spirit Stone"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SPIRIT_STONE_TITLE"
msgstr "Spirit Stone"

#. world_info.csv: The world undergoes celestial changes (such as ...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_WORLD_QI_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The world undergoes celestial changes (such as Qi Tides) every few years, "
"affecting character abilities."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_WORLD_QI_NAME"
msgstr "World Qi"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_WORLD_QI_TITLE"
msgstr "World Qi"

#. world_info.csv: The cultivation world features the Heaven, Eart...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_RANKING_DESC"
msgstr "The cultivation world features the Heaven, Earth, and Human Rankings, as well as the Sect Ranking. The three personal rankings are grouped by equivalent standard realm: Heaven records Nascent Soul-tier experts, Earth records Core Formation-tier experts, and Human records Foundation Establishment-tier experts. The Sect Ranking ranks sects by total power."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_RANKING_NAME"
msgstr "Ranking"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_RANKING_TITLE"
msgstr "Ranking"

#. world_info.csv: Mortal dynasties rule the realm, maintaining wo...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_DYNASTY_DESC"
msgstr "Mortal dynasties rule the realm, maintaining worldly order and borders. Emperors live no longer than ordinary mortals, and when one dies, a new emperor succeeds to the throne."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_DYNASTY_NAME"
msgstr "Dynasty"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_DYNASTY_TITLE"
msgstr "Dynasty"

#. world_info.csv: Cultivators may govern for the imperial court, ...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_OFFICIAL_DESC"
msgstr "Cultivators may govern for the imperial court, building court reputation and receiving salary. With enough reputation they can be promoted; the higher the office, the greater the salary and luck. If they neglect governance for too long, their reputation will gradually decline."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_OFFICIAL_NAME"
msgstr "Official Rank"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_OFFICIAL_TITLE"
msgstr "Official Rank"

#. world_info.csv: The same cultivation ranks have different names in each tradition.
msgid "WORLD_INFO_CULTIVATION_ALIAS_DESC"
msgstr "The same cultivation ranks have different names in each tradition: Daoists and rogue cultivators use Qi Refinement, Foundation Establishment, Core Formation, and Nascent Soul; martial cultivators use Body Tempering, Tendon-Tempering, Martial Master, and Martial Saint; Confucian cultivators use Vital Qi Cultivation, Principle Illumination, Mandate Establishment, and Great Scholar; Buddhist cultivators use Novice Monk, Monk, Arhat, and Bodhisattva; yao cultivators use Spirit Awakening, Form Transformation, Demon Core, and Demon King. These names map to the same underlying realm sequence; they change narrative and interface wording, but not breakthrough, power, lifespan, item grade, or other rules."

#. world_info.csv: Realm Aliases
msgid "WORLD_INFO_CULTIVATION_ALIAS_NAME"
msgstr "Realm Aliases"

#. world_info.csv: Realm Aliases
msgid "WORLD_INFO_CULTIVATION_ALIAS_TITLE"
msgstr "Realm Aliases"

#. world_info.csv: Gu arts require a cultivator to carry a Gu tool...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_GU_DESC"
msgstr "Gu arts require a cultivator to carry a Gu tool and have the ability to inflict Gu before applying it to an observable target. Different Gu act in different ways: Mind-Sinking Gu subtly shifts relationships, Blood-Devouring Gu periodically damages life, while Essence-Eroding Gu and Heart-Disordering Gu disturb cultivation. Inflicting Gu has a success rate affected by the tool, the caster's bonuses, and the target's Gu resistance; failure may be detected and harm the relationship."

#. world_info.csv:
msgid "WORLD_INFO_GU_NAME"
msgstr "Gu"

#. world_info.csv: Gu
msgid "WORLD_INFO_GU_TITLE"
msgstr "Gu"

#. world_info.csv: Formations require a cultivator to carry a form...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_FORMATION_DESC"
msgstr "Formations require a cultivator to carry a formation disk and have formation-setting ability before placing a temporary regional effect at the current location. Different formations suit different regions: cultivation grounds and sect regions can hold spirit-gathering, mountain-guarding, clarity, and similar arrays; cities can hold healing arrays; mines, herb fields, and beast domains can hold vein-seeking, wood-growth, and beast-driving arrays. Formations consume spirit stones and expire after their duration ends."

#. world_info.csv:
msgid "WORLD_INFO_FORMATION_NAME"
msgstr "Formations"

#. world_info.csv: Formations
msgid "WORLD_INFO_FORMATION_TITLE"
msgstr "Formations"

#. world_info.csv: Cultivators may occasionally feel a sudden stir...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_OPPORTUNITY_DESC"
msgstr "Cultivators may occasionally feel a sudden stir of fate, sensing that a person or place is tied to their own opportunity. If they follow the sense, they may gain treasure or a boon, return empty-handed, or meet danger; if they delay too long, the opportunity fades away."

#. world_info.csv:
msgid "WORLD_INFO_OPPORTUNITY_NAME"
msgstr "Opportunity"

#. world_info.csv: Opportunity
msgid "WORLD_INFO_OPPORTUNITY_TITLE"
msgstr "Opportunity"
